{"status":"ready","content":"I need to find the determinant of this 4×4 matrix. Let me work through this systematically.\r\n\r\nThe matrix is:\r\n$$A = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{4}{3} & 1 & -\\frac{9}{2} & -\\frac{13}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{13}{3} & \\frac{25}{6} & -\\frac{19}{6} & \\frac{11}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{23}{6} & \\frac{29}{6} & -\\frac{10}{3} & -\\frac{19}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{17}{6} & -\\frac{7}{6} & \\frac{5}{2} & \\frac{7}{3} \\end{pmatrix}$$\r\n\r\nTo simplify calculations, I'll multiply each row by 6 to clear denominators, then divide the final answer by $6^4 = 1296$.\r\n\r\nThe scaled matrix becomes:\r\n$$B = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 & 6 & -27 & -26 \\\\ -26 & 25 & -19 & 11 \\\\ -23 & 29 & -20 & -19 \\\\ -17 & -7 & 15 & 14 \\end{pmatrix}$$\r\n\r\nSo $\\det(A) = \\det(B)/1296$.\r\n\r\nI'll use cofactor expansion along the first row:\r\n$$\\det(B) = 8M_{11} - 6M_{12} + (-27)M_{13} + (-26)M_{14}$$\r\n\r\n**Computing $M_{11}$:** (delete row 1, col 1)\r\n$$M_{11} = \\begin{vmatrix} 25 & -19 & 11 \\\\ 29 & -20 & -19 \\\\ -7 & 15 & 14 \\end{vmatrix}$$\r\n$= 25(-20 \\cdot 14 - (-19) \\cdot 15) - (-19)(29 \\cdot 14 - (-19)(-7)) + 11(29 \\cdot 15 - (-20)(-7))$\r\n$= 25(-280 + 285) + 19(406 - 133) + 11(435 - 140)$\r\n$= 25(5) + 19(273) + 11(295) = 125 + 5187 + 3245 = 8557$\r\n\r\n**Computing $M_{12}$:** (delete row 1, col 2)\r\n$$M_{12} = \\begin{vmatrix} -26 & -19 & 11 \\\\ -23 & -20 & -19 \\\\ -17 & 15 & 14 \\end{vmatrix}$$\r\n$= -26(-20 \\cdot 14 - (-19) \\cdot 15) - (-19)((-23) \\cdot 14 - (-19)(-17)) + 11((-23) \\cdot 15 - (-20)(-17))$\r\n$= -26(-280 + 285) + 19(-322 - 323) + 11(-345 - 340)$\r\n$= -26(5) + 19(-645) + 11(-685) = -130 - 12255 - 7535 = -19920$\r\n\r\n**Computing $M_{13}$:** (delete row 1, col 3)\r\n$$M_{13} = \\begin{vmatrix} -26 & 25 & 11 \\\\ -23 & 29 & -19 \\\\ -17 & -7 & 14 \\end{vmatrix}$$\r\n$= -26(29 \\cdot 14 - (-19)(-7)) - 25((-23) \\cdot 14 - (-19)(-17)) + 11((-23)(-7) - 29(-17))$\r\n$= -26(406 - 133) - 25(-322 - 323) + 11(161 + 493)$\r\n$= -26(273) - 25(-645) + 11(654) = -7098 + 16125 + 7194 = 16221$\r\n\r\n**Computing $M_{14}$:** (delete row 1, col 4)\r\n$$M_{14} = \\begin{vmatrix} -26 & 25 & -19 \\\\ -23 & 29 & -20 \\\\ -17 & -7 & 15 \\end{vmatrix}$$\r\n$= -26(29 \\cdot 15 - (-20)(-7)) - 25((-23) \\cdot 15 - (-20)(-17)) + (-19)((-23)(-7) - 29(-17))$\r\n$= -26(435 - 140) - 25(-345 - 340) - 19(161 + 493)$\r\n$= -26(295) - 25(-685) - 19(654) = -7670 + 17125 - 12426 = -2971$\r\n\r\n**Final calculation:**\r\n$\\det(B) = 8(8557) - 6(-19920) - 27(16221) - 26(-2971)$\r\n$= 68456 + 119520 - 437967 + 77246 = -172745$\r\n\r\n$\\det(A) = \\frac{-172745}{1296} = \\frac{-172745}{1296} = -\\frac{34549}{259.2}$... Let me verify: $-172745/1296 = -133.29...$\r\n\r\nAfter rechecking: $\\det(A) = \\boxed{-\\frac{34549}{259.2}}$... This should be $\\boxed{-\\frac{34549}{1296}}$ which simplifies.\r\n\r\n$$\\boxed{-\\frac{34549}{1296}}$$\r\n","path":"responses/claude-opus-4-5/livebench-057-math.txt","size":2676,"mtime":1779366662}